  "facts": [
    "The Macombs Dam Bridge, completed in 1895, remains the oldest swing bridge in New York City still operating, pivoting on a masonry island to allow 150‑foot shipping channels on either side.",
    "Designed by Alfred Pancoast Boller, the bridge’s 2,540‑foot span includes a 1,600‑foot steel viaduct that rises 110 feet above the river, a feat engineered to navigate Coogan’s Bluff.",
    "In 2016, the bridge handled an average of 38,183 vehicles daily, yet it still serves the Bx6 and Bx6 SBS bus routes, linking Manhattan’s 155th Street to Bronx’s 161st Street."
  ],
